I’d like to be able to answer that question and my answers won’t seem so weird. If you want to look it up, here’s a summary of why. A lot of reasons to use stories are:

Cultures tell stories to give an interpretation;

Cultures tell stories to be read or memorized;

Cultures tell stories to be told;

Cultures tell stories to keep a status quo;

Cultures tell stories to make sense;

Cultures tell stories to control the narrative;

Cultures tell stories to make the story better; and

Cultures tell stories to gain power and prestige.

But all of these have their detractors.

